# L §3.1 (PL-17): "A position that takes a code takes any expression of the code's type, such as a read of an input
# that holds one (MODE, in flows … at and prorata, takes a code word or such a read, §2.3)." prorata's mode is the input
# md: half-up gives 100.00 * 1/3 = 33.33 and 100.00 * 2/3 = 66.67 PLN (q1); pinned to down, 33.33 PLN (q2). round's
# mode and add_business's calendar from inputs too (r: 10.00 / 3 = 3.333... half-up = 3.33 PLN; nb: the business day after
# Friday 2026-01-02 under weekends [sat, sun] is Monday 2026-01-05).
=== m.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index parts = [a, b, c]
input total: money PLN
input w[p in parts]: num
input md: rounding
input x: money PLN
input n: int
input cal: calendar
input d0: date

def share_list[p in parts]: money PLN = prorata(total, w[j] for j in [a, b], p, minor(PLN), md, rest none)
def r: money PLN = round(x / n, minor(PLN), md) at reader
def nb: date = add_business(d0, 1, cal) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  total = 100.00 PLN
  w[a] = 1
  w[b] = 2
  w[c] = 3
  md = half-up
  x = 10.00 PLN
  n = 3
  d0 = 2026-01-02
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])

ask q1: share_list[p] for p in [a, b]
ask q2: share_list[a] with md = down
ask q3: r, nb law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1 (p = a): 33.33 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q1 (p = b): 66.67 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q2: 33.33 PLN
  pinned: md = down
  cut 2026-10-20
q3: (3.33 PLN, 2026-01-05)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-20
